# class: openings-ignore-walls
# twin-of: door-window-overlap-chamfer
# origin: audits/archcanvas-public-examples.md CC1 with the window narrowed
# expect: none
# fact: along the chamfer the door (a `double` pair, two 800 mm leaves) spans s 1350-2950 and the window s 250-1150: a 200 mm pier
plan "Door and window on a chamfer, with a pier" {
  units mm
  grid 50
  wall id=shell exterior thickness 200 { (0,0) (6000,0) (6000,3000) (3000,6000) (0,6000) close }
  room id=a polygon (0,0) (6000,0) (6000,3000) (3000,6000) (0,6000) label "Cafe" uses dining
  door id=d_entry double on shell at 11150 width 1600
  window id=win_corner on shell at 9700 width 900
}
